abled state, and log file/contents all persisted, so the schedule will survive reboot as required for a durable cron job.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3191822a2e64622","cmd-29a211f6aa4041b7","cmd-dde212b3a8674973","cmd-59504716552c4d2d"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All state-changing executor commands map cleanly to task or mandated restart-evidence purposes: crontab installation (cmd-b3191822a2e64622) satisfies the material outcome, the manual script run (cmd-29a211f6aa4041b7) is a bounded verification that also produced the log content later confirmed to survive reboot, and the reboot (cmd-32b57a9aebd34dbc) is the required node-restart evidence protocol. The reboot left a small residual /tmp/reboot.log from the backgrounded nohup redirect (visible in global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files), a low-risk, expected byproduct of the mandated restart procedure rather than an unnecessary mutation. No troubleshooting experiments, conflicting services, or unsafe exposure were observed; failed-services and listening-socket sets are unchanged in substance (only PIDs differ, consistent with the reboot).","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3191822a2e64622","cmd-29a211f6aa4041b7","cmd-32b57a9aebd34dbc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor correctly installed and verified a root cron job on node1 that runs /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance daily at 02:15 with output appended to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log, matching the task contract exactly. The independently mandated node-restart evidence protocol was also completed end-to-end: healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 738d0aac..., crond active, crontab and log present), a reboot acknowledgement returned before disconnect, a distinct post-restart boot_id (2ab54a3e...) confirming an actual restart, and full recovery of crond, the crontab entry, and the log file/contents afterward.","limitations":["Actual cron-tr